{"question": "Write a Java method `firstNonRepeatedChar(String s)` that returns the first character that appears exactly once in the string, or '\0' if none exists, using a HashMap for O(n) time.", "starter_code": "public static char firstNonRepeatedChar(String s) {
    // TODO
}", "answer": "public static char firstNonRepeatedChar(String s) {
    Map<Character, Integer> counts = new HashMap<>();
    for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
        counts.put(c, counts.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
    }
    for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
        if (counts.get(c) == 1) {
            return c;
        }
    }
    return '\0';
}", "explanation": "The first pass builds a frequency map in O(n); the second pass walks the string again in original order and returns the first character whose count is exactly 1, giving overall O(n) time.", "concepts": ["hashmap", "strings", "frequency count"]}

